-- cmd: repl
-- stdin: fn down(n: Int) -> Int {\n  match n {\n    0 -> 0\n    _ -> down(n - 1)\n  }\n}\nfn run() -> Int { down(3) }\nrun()\nfn down(n: Int) -> Int {\n  match n {\n    0 -> 1 / n\n    _ -> down(n - 1)\n  }\n}\nrun()\n:quit\n
-- A function that calls itself in tail position, defined again: the new
-- body runs, every round (a call of the old one's callers too), and the
-- call stack of its error is that of the new one.
